     c: 'Peng Dehuai 彭德怀 writes "Notes on reading the Center''s urgent directive" 《读中共中央紧急指示的笔记》: basically good, the return of private plots and houses and the end of the "communist wind" heartening; but it keeps the public mess halls 公共食堂, born of "eating without paying," which waste the cadres'' strength, and while they stand the peasants'' zeal will not revive; it says nothing of the imbalances, boasting and coercion since 1958, and is only the start of correcting the errors. A Communist, he should put this to the Center; but after the Lushan 庐山 meeting and the Eighth Plenum 八届八中全会 it would do no good and might be misread: better to read on, and ask to be sent down to the villages to labor and investigate.'
