e a coup; "every sentence of Chairman Mao''s is truth, one worth ten thousand of ours"); [[w.jian-zhou-enlai]], 541 (Lin on the danger of a "reactionary coup d''état"; "one word of Mao''s counts for ten thousand words of others"; "whoever opposes Mao will be put to death by the whole party and cursed by the whole country"); [[w.teiwes-tragedy-of-lin-biao]], 60–63 (the speech, with "the smell of gunpowder," on coups in Asia, Africa and Latin America and in Chinese dynasties, applied to Peng, Luo, Lu and Yang; Lin "ha[d] not thought much about this problem," but Mao, sleepless, had called in comrades on preventing coups and posted men at the radio stations, the army and public security; Lin not alone in drafting it: by the *Renmin ribao* of May 18, 1978, Zhang Chunqiao worked on the coup formula, which the authors doubt, 62 n.10; Mao approves its circulation within the Party); [[w.dikotter-cultural-revolution]], 50 n.20 (Lin reads out the accusation, prepared by Kang Sheng on Mao''s orders: "a bunch of bastards" who want to kill us; "Isn''t Chairman Mao a genius?"; Zhou: "I entirely agree with comrade Lin''s words"); [[w.pu-weihua-zalan-jiu-shijie]], 82–87 (the morning of May 18, the "coup classic": Mao these months watching against a counter-revolutionary coup, men and troops moved, radio stations guarded; Peng, Luo, Lu and Yang linked; Mao''s genius; whoever opposes him, the whole Party and country to strike him down; the Center forwards it Sept. 22, 1966, its notice quoted, 86–87); [[w.chen-yun-nianpu-xiuding]], III, 153 (Lin Biao''s long speech: Peng Zhen, Luo Ruiqing, Lu Dingyi and others plotted a coup and subversion; Mao''s genius; "whoever opposes him the whole Party will punish, the whole country attack"); [[w.zhu-de-nianpu-xinbian]], III, 1952 (May 18, 1966; Lin Biao 林彪 speaks at the meeting, pressing the cult of Mao Zedong''s person and, gathering cases ancient and modern, Chinese and foreign, making up the lie that some are plotting a coup). Made public: 1