@@ -2841,7 +2841,7 @@ entries:
     follows:
       - cal.1966-10-16.china-leadership-3
     c: 'Chen Boda reads to a plenary session of the Central Work Conference, in the Great Hall of the People, his report "Two Lines in the Great Proletarian Cultural Revolution," which Mao revised repeatedly before and after its delivery. Its four sections: the situation is "excellent"; the continuing two-line struggle and the lingering impact of the bourgeois reactionary line, with some children of high officials as Red Guards claiming to be successors by birthright, against Mao Zedong Thought, and some "about to embark on a revisionist road"; the "fearful" faction, wrong to think the masses are acting recklessly; and the Red Guards, to adhere to Mao''s class line and unite the majority.'
-    n: '[[w.macfarquhar-maos-last-revolution]], 136–137; [[w.mao-zedong-zhuan]], VI, ch. 75 n.17 (Oct. 16 Chen Boda''s long speech ''Two lines in the proletarian cultural revolution'', the conference''s main report: the struggle of the two lines goes on, the Sixteen Points corrected the earlier bourgeois line, but a wrong line may take other forms; some, a few, comrades think themselves old revolutionaries, are officials and gentry, forget their revolutionary history, and will not let the masses touch them; ''a handful'' of power-holders on the capitalist road and many muddled; printed with Mao''s approval; the day of the printing not given, n.17). [[w.yang-jisheng-tiandi-fanfu]], I, 300 (Oct. 16 Chen Boda gives for the Center the main report, 〈無產階級文化大革命中的兩條路線〉, later retitled "summing up two months of the movement"; Mao had told Chen his thoughts before; the report praises the movement of the preceding stretch and the masses'' rebellion, finds the situation excellent, analyzes the new forms of the bourgeois reactionary line, criticizes the beating of rebels as counter-revolutionaries and the "blood-line theory": "why must the children of high cadres hold the power? is their blood noble?"; asks the cadres to drop fear and let the masses go; criticizes sectarianism put in place of the class line); [[w.jian-zhou-enlai]], 553–554 (Chen Boda''s keynote, revised and approved by Mao: the two-line struggles of the Party''s history complicated and fierce; dispel fear, mobilize the masses, deepen the Cultural Revolution); [[w.dikotter-cultural-revolution]], 116 n.5 (Chen Boda names Liu Shaoqi and Deng Xiaoping the main targets, sets their "bourgeois reactionary line" against Mao''s line, and savages Tan Lifu''s bloodline couplet; the talk widely disseminated on Mao''s instructions); [[w.pu-weihua-zalan-jiu-shijie]], 215 (in his report Chen Boda names Tan Lifu''s views and criticizes him severely; afterward Chen Boda, Jiang Qing, Kang Sheng, Zhang Chunqiao, Yao Wenyuan, Wang